@page "/privacy"
@inject Translator L

<PageTitle>@L["Privacy"] · Alfar Quest</PageTitle>

<article class="aq-doc">
    <h1>@L["Privacy"]</h1>

    <p class="aq-doc-lede">
        @L["What this game stores about you, in plain words. This is a description of the implementation, not a lawyer's document — read it as a technical statement."]
    </p>

    <h2>@L["What is stored"]</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>@L["Your name, email address, and — if you gave them — country and phone number."]</li>
        <li>@L["A one-way hash of your password. The password itself is never stored, and cannot be recovered from the hash."]</li>
        <li>@L["Your avatar, if you upload one, re-encoded to a 256px PNG."]</li>
        <li>@L["When you registered, when you last signed in, and one row per active session."]</li>
        <li>@L["Your game statistics: highest level, gold and time played."]</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>@L["What is not stored"]</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>@L["Your password in any readable form."]</li>
        <li>@L["Anything from third-party trackers or analytics — there are none in this application."]</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>@L["Sessions"]</h2>
    <p>
        @L["Signing in stores a random token in your browser. It is not your password and carries no personal information. Signing out revokes it on the server, so it cannot be used again by anyone who has a copy."]
    </p>

    <p class="aq-doc-foot"><a class="aq-link" href="/">@L["Back to the gate"]</a></p>
</article>
